{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And what are we, that you murmur against us</b> Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 16:7): וְנַחְנוּ מַה — it is in our hands to do, for we have done only what He commanded us. But this is not so; rather, it is like \"what is man that You remember him\" (Psalms 8:5), \"what is man that You know him\" (ibid. 144:3), \"for in what is he to be accounted\" (Isaiah 2:22). And this is the way of humility: what are we, that you should hang it upon us that we brought you out of the land of Egypt? We are nothing and our deeds are vanity. And <b>your murmurings are not against us but against HaShem</b> — it is He who brings you out of the land of Egypt, not us. And in the Mekhilta (here): and what are we, that we should be plastered over while you stand and rebel against us?"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase סְפוּנִים in the Mekhilta citation is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'plastered over' (from the root ספן) following its apparent sense of being covered or concealed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:09:14.110974358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}